# Version bump → commit → push

Whenever recognition/logic changes ship with a new **versionCode** / **versionName** bump in `app/build.gradle.kts`:

1. Finish the code change and bump the version (every testable build needs a distinguishable version).
2. **Commit and push in the same turn** — do not leave a bumped version uncommitted or unpushed.
3. Do not wait for the user to ask separately; bumping the version means the round is ready to ship to device.

Commit message: short imperative summary + `(vX.Y.Z)` in the title, optional body with what to verify on Evaluate.

Do not skip push after commit. If the user explicitly says not to push, commit locally only and say so.
